{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/630738-alternate-sources-of-blood-magic","id":630738,"title":"Alternate sources of blood magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-17T23:28:56-07:00","id":630738,"title":"Alternate sources of blood magic","content":"So if I was a vampire who wanted to learn blood magic and saw what it could do and thus had beleif in it, but did not like the lancea sanctum or circle of the crone how would they learn, could they invent their own form of blood magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","user":"Andresmo23","date":". 08-18-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T02:23:27-07:00","id":630878,"title":"","content":"Circle of the Crime- now that's a pretty badass name for any given group. <br /> <br /> Jokes aside, yes the Covenants do not share their most potent secrets to outsiders, so you won't get anything out of them. You could steal their secrets, but then they'd have you murdered next week.<br /> <br /> Maybe a sufficiently knowledgeable and powerful vampire could observe both forms sorcery from the Covenants to glean a working principle? After all, that's exactly what the founders of the Lancea et Sanctum did to create Theban Sorcery. Also, the Circle of the Crone is a vampiric Neo-Pagan cult that built itself out of disparate cults whose claims of descent from 'true' Pagan practices are dubious at best- so their arts of Cr\u00faac is already a cobble of rituals from various sources. <br /> <br /> For some tangible inspiration, many people on here homebrewed and posted various forms of Blood Sorcery already. You could pick one, tweak them to your needs, and build an in-universe history of how those rituals came to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:58:17-07:00","id":630932,"title":"","content":"One could invent something mechanically the same as Cruac with a different flavor which might or might not be actual Cruac (interchangeable). Cruac seems to be the more intuitive blood sorcery. I think a variant of Theban would need to steeped in some mortal religion and given by divine intervention, yada yada yada. It is harder to justify something like Theban without roots to mortal institutions because it is more sorcery, less blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:07:57-07:00","id":630993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andresmo23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/630738-alternate-sources-of-blood-magic#post630738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I was a vampire who wanted to learn blood magic and saw what it could do and thus had beleif in it, but did not like the lancea sanctum or circle of the crime how would they learn, could they invent their own form of blood magic</div> </div> </div> </div> There's the Architects of the Monolith, with their Gilded Cage magic. Voodoo uses its own system. There was a magic sorcery for blood poisons in the Ancient Bloodlines book. Veneficia, despite using the same rotes as Cruac, is actually a wildly different in practice.<br /> <br /> Different sorceries happen fairly often.<br /> <br /> How do you make these other soriceries? Through plot and possibly bloodline refinements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:08:14-07:00","id":631250,"title":"","content":"There was a Blood Sorcery supplement that came out just before 2nd edition that has ideas of creating alternate cruacs and Theban style sorcries.<br /> I need to get a copy and do my own revision. The 2nd editon rituals were built with its theme system in mind. However I heard secret of covenants does not follow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:56:43-07:00","id":638555,"title":"","content":"Let's see. In addition to Theban Sorcery and Cr\u00faac, there is:<br /> <br /> <b>Ahranite Sorcery:</b> VII p. 35; Secret rituals of the Akhud, available to members of VII in games where &quot;<i>Princes of the Fallen City</i>&quot; is true.<br /> <b>Lithopedia:</b> Night Horrors: Immortal Sinner p. 118; Formerly Cr\u00faac rituals, but they were divorced when the founder of Csal\u00e1d formed his bloodline. Functions similarly to Cr\u00faac.<br /> <b>M\u00e9rges Sorcery:</b> Ancient Bloodlines p. 147; The aforementioned poison-based ritual form, also deals heavily in emotion<br /> <b>Sethite Cr\u00faac:</b> Shadows in the Dark: Mekhet, p. 92; Another branch of Cr\u00faac, following the ideals of the chaos-obsessed followers of <i>Typhon-Seth</i>.<br /> <b>Veneficia:</b> Requiem for Rome p. 114; An ancient form of Cr\u00faac that shares many rituals, but is decidedly more Hellenistic in its symbolism<br /> <b>Vodoun:</b> Ancient Bloodlines p. 73; A form of Blood Sorcery that involves consorting with spirits called <i>Loa</i>, and splitting into three distinct branches, Ghede (necromancy), Kalfou (hexes) and Papa Legba (controlling spirits)<br /> <br /> And two disciplines that resemble Blood Sorcery, but aren't quite the same. If using Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies, they could be easily adapted:<br /> <b>Ortam:</b> Bloodlines: The Legendary p. 75; Vampiric Aromatherapy<br /> <b>Spoiling:</b> Ordo Dracul p. 204; Poisons that weaken attributes or deliver effects to imbibers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:39:01-07:00","id":639125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/630738-alternate-sources-of-blood-magic?p=630878#post630878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circle of the Crime- now that's a pretty badass name for any given group.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, yes the Covenants do not share their most potent secrets to outsiders, so you won't get anything out of them. You could steal their secrets, but then they'd have you murdered next week.<br /> <br /> Maybe a sufficiently knowledgeable and powerful vampire could observe both forms sorcery from the Covenants to glean a working principle? After all, that's exactly what the founders of the Lancea et Sanctum did to create Theban Sorcery. Also, the Circle of the Crone is a vampiric Neo-Pagan cult that built itself out of disparate cults whose claims of descent from 'true' Pagan practices are dubious at best- so their arts of Cr\u00faac is already a cobble of rituals from various sources.<br /> <br /> For some tangible inspiration, many people on here homebrewed and posted various forms of Blood Sorcery already. You could pick one, tweak them to your needs, and build an in-universe history of how those rituals came to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeeeaah, I don't see a religious group who believs their magic is a gift from god responding very well to a non believer wielding such power out in the open. The second you show off Theban Sorcery, you'd be branded a heretic and blasphemer.<br /> <br /> As for Cruac, it's easier to get a hold of than Thaumaturgy was, since the Circle is a covenant that any clan can join, instead of being a clan of its own. But even then, it seems like Cruac is focused around pagan rituals and occult secrets, which implies it too has some religious implications.<br /> <br /> At any rate, you need to be like rank 2 (I think?) in either covenant before they'll pass on their secrets, which means you need to have spent time and worked your way up in status. By that time, you're likely to be recognizable as a member, so learning both powers freely would be very difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}